{"source_id":"arXiv:1404.6879","title":"\\LargeQuantization of the shift of argument subalgebras in type $A$","abstract":"Given a simple Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{g}$ and an element $μ\\in\\mathfrak{g}^*$, the corresponding shift of argument subalgebra of $\\text{S}(\\mathfrak{g})$ is Poisson commutative. In the case where $μ$ is regular, this subalgebra is known to admit a quantization, that is, it can be lifted to a commutative subalgebra of $\\text{U}(\\mathfrak{g})$. We show that if $\\mathfrak{g}$ is of type $A$, then this property extends to arbitrary $μ$, thus proving a conjecture of Feigin, Frenkel and Toledano Laredo. The proof relies on an explicit construction of generators of the center of the affine vertex algebra at the critical level.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev"],"year":"2014","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.6879","doi":"10.48550/arXiv.1404.6879","cluster":"representation_theory","cards":[{"card_id":"ma-c-6f9d94bc3d68ec817b0b","label":"Abstract","kind":"abstract","line":191,"snippet":"Given a simple Lie algebra $\\g$ and an element $\\mu\\in\\g^*$, the corresponding shift of argument subalgebra of $\\Sr(\\g)$ is Poisson commutative. In the case where $\\mu$ is regular, this subalgebra is …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-fb8c04eeedbac0d83008","label":"Equation killi","kind":"equation","line":329,"snippet":"\\langle X,Y\\rangle=\\frac{1}{2\\tss h^{\\vee}}\\ts\\tr\\ts(\\ad\\tss X\\ts\\ad\\tss Y),"},{"card_id":"ma-c-e105d19e7a2d02499137","label":"Equation genz","kind":"equation","line":382,"snippet":"\\z(\\wh\\g)=\\CC[T^{\\tss r}S_l | l=1,\\dots,n, r\\geqslant 0],"},{"card_id":"ma-c-52ddd1d41e800cf16d16","label":"Equation evalr","kind":"equation","line":402,"snippet":"\\varrho^{}_{\\ts\\mu,z}:\\U(t^{-1}\\g[t^{-1}])\\to \\U(\\g), X[r]\\mapsto X z^r+\\de_{r,-1}\\ts\\mu(X), X\\in\\g,"},{"card_id":"ma-c-1ed3fc6ea865a1c2989a","label":"Equation rhoexp","kind":"equation","line":415,"snippet":"\\varrho^{}_{\\ts\\mu,z}(S)=S^{(0)} z^{-d}+\\dots+S^{(d-1)}